    }
  }

  slide "Locust: master/worker distribution" {
    eyebrow: "Locust architecture"
    title: "MasterRunner distributes users; UsersDispatcher decides how"
    lede: "MasterRunner spawns no greenlets itself — it directs WorkerRunner processes over ZeroMQ ROUTER/DEALER sockets (msgpack-encoded Message envelopes). UsersDispatcher round-robins workers via itertools.cycle and draws user classes from a Kullback-Leibler-weighted generator."

    narration: "MasterRunner's own docstring says it plainly: it doesn't spawn any user greenlets itself, it expects WorkerRunners to connect, then directs them to start and stop user greenlets. The wire protocol underneath is ZeroMQ — the master binds a ROUTER socket, each worker connects a DEALER socket identified by its client ID, and every message is a small (message_type, data, node_id) envelope serialized with msgpack. To decide which worker gets the next simulated user, UsersDispatcher keeps an itertools.cycle over pre-sorted worker nodes and just takes the next one each time — a plain round robin. Which user CLASS to place next, independent of worker, comes from a Kullback-Leibler divergence generator that yields class names in proportion to their configured weight, so a 5:1 weight ratio produces an interleaved pattern like AAABAAAAABAA rather than five in a row then one."

    term: {
      word: "UsersDispatcher"
      meaning: "Locust's algorithm for deciding, on a MasterRunner, which worker process and which User subclass receives the next simulated user during ramp-up: itertools.cycle for round-robin worker placement, a KL-divergence generator for weighted user-class interleaving."
    }

    points: [
      "MasterRunner docstring: \"doesn't spawn any user greenlets itself\" — directs WorkerRunners instead (runners.py:653-656).",
      "Wire protocol: ZeroMQ ROUTER (master) / DEALER (worker), Message(type, data, node_id) serialized with msgpack (rpc/zmqrpc.py, rpc/protocol.py:32-47).",
      "Worker placement: itertools.cycle(sorted worker nodes) — plain round robin (dispatch.py:105).",
      "User-class placement: a Kullback-Leibler divergence generator weighted by User.weight (dispatch.py:26-44)."
    ]

    caption: "ZeroMQ ROUTER/DEALER envelopes; round-robin workers, KL-weighted user classes."

    render: @scene {
