  slide "Locust: stats merge and stop semantics" {
    eyebrow: "Locust architecture"
    title: "Stats push every 3.0s; stop drains only between tasks"
    lede: "Every worker pushes its own already-aggregated stats to the master every WORKER_REPORT_INTERVAL (3.0s), and the master merges them by calling extend() on its running total. Stopping is a real drain, but only if --stop-timeout is set, and only up to the next task boundary."

    narration: "WorkerRunner.stats_reporter loops forever: send stats, then gevent.sleep(3.0). Each report already contains that worker's own aggregated StatsEntry objects; the master doesn't recompute from raw samples, it calls stats.total.extend() to merge each worker's total into its own running total roughly every three seconds. On stopping, Locust does have a genuine core drain mechanism, not just a user-script convenience: if environment.stop_timeout is set, a running greenlet's state flips to STOPPING and TaskSet.run()'s loop checks that flag and raises StopUser after the CURRENT task returns — not immediately. The master then waits up to stop_timeout, plus a 60-second safety margin, for every worker's user count to actually reach zero before proceeding. But that protection has an exact edge documented in User.wait()'s own docstring: if a greenlet happens to be inside wait() — sleeping between tasks — when the stop signal arrives, it's killed immediately regardless of stop_timeout, because there's no task in progress to let finish. And if stop_timeout isn't set at all, every greenlet is killed immediately via gevent.Greenlet.kill(), full stop, no exceptions."

    term: {
      word: "stop_timeout drain"
      meaning: "Locust's core (not user-script) graceful-stop mechanism: when set, a stopping User finishes its current task before exiting, bounded by stop_timeout seconds. It does not protect a User that is currently inside wait() when the stop signal arrives — that greenlet is killed immediately regardless."
    }

    points: [
      "stats_reporter: send_stats() then gevent.sleep(WORKER_REPORT_INTERVAL=3.0) forever — runners.py:1450-1456.",
      "Master merges via stats.total.extend(unserialized worker total) — stats.py:792-806, incremental merge not full recompute.",
      "With --stop-timeout: stop signal sets STOPPING; TaskSet checks it and raises StopUser only after the current task returns.",
      "Without --stop-timeout, or if the greenlet is inside wait() at stop time: immediate gevent.Greenlet.kill(), no drain at all."
    ]

    caption: "Report every 3s, merge incrementally; drain protects the task, not the wait."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s4-hdr",
        title = "3.0s STATS PUSH · BOUNDED DRAIN",
        caption = "Report every 3s, merge incrementally; drain protects the task, not the wait.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.secondary),
        inkRole = theme(ink.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s4-worker",
        title = "Worker stats_reporter",
        detail = "send → sleep(3.0) → repeat",
        x = 60, y = 100, width = 240, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s4-e1",
        mode = "connector",
        from = { nodeId: "s4-worker", anchor: "e" },
        to = { nodeId: "s4-merge", anchor: "w" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.tertiary), strokeWidth: 2.2 }
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s4-merge",
        title = "stats.total.extend()",
        detail = "incremental merge on master",
        x = 400, y = 100, width = 240, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.tertiary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s4-inTask",
        title = "In a task",
        detail = "stop_timeout: finishes, then exits",
        x = 60, y = 230, width = 260, height = 70,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.green)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s4-inWait",
        title = "In wait()",
        detail = "killed immediately, no exception",
        x = 380, y = 230, width = 260, height = 70,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.warning)
      )
      sdk.Note(
        id = "s4-note",
        text = "No --stop-timeout at all: every greenlet killed immediately, in a task or not",
        x = 60, y = 330, width = 580, height = 30
      )
      sdk.Signal(
        id = "s4-motion",
        from = { nodeId: "s4-inTask", anchor: "center" },
        to = { nodeId: "s4-inWait", anchor: "center" },
        opacity = 0.4,
        strokeWidth = 2,
        label = "protected vs not",
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.warning) }
      )

      timeline main {
        at 0 reveal s4-hdr duration 260
        after s4-hdr reveal s4-worker duration 260
        after s4-worker trace s4-e1 duration 280
        after s4-e1 reveal s4-merge duration 260
