  slide "AIPerf: ZMQ socket topology" {
    eyebrow: "AIPerf architecture"
    title: "Five distinct socket patterns for five different jobs"
    lede: "One XPUB/XSUB event bus for pub/sub messaging, a DEALER/ROUTER proxy for on-demand dataset requests, a PUSH/PULL proxy for raw inference results — all three hosted inside SystemController — plus a ROUTER/DEALER credit dispatch channel and a dedicated PUSH/PULL credit-return channel, both bound directly inside timing_manager."

    narration: "AIPerf doesn't use one ZMQ pattern for everything — it picks the pattern that matches each job. Broadcast-style status and lifecycle messages ride an XPUB/XSUB event bus that every service publishes to and subscribes from. Workers occasionally need to ask the dataset manager for a conversation on demand, so that's a DEALER/ROUTER request-reply proxy. Raw inference results stream from workers toward the record-processing pipeline as fire-and-forget PUSH/PULL. Credit dispatch specifically is not proxied at all — timing_manager's StickyCreditRouter binds a ROUTER socket directly, and each worker connects a DEALER socket carrying its own identity, so the router can address a credit to one specific worker. Credit returns ride their own separate PUSH/PULL channel rather than going back over the same ROUTER, so the dispatch direction never has to double as a return path."

    term: {
      word: "CommAddress"
      meaning: "AIPerf's enum of every distinct logical ZMQ address in the system (EVENT_BUS_PROXY_FRONTEND/BACKEND, CREDIT_ROUTER, CREDIT_RETURN, DATASET_MANAGER_PROXY_FRONTEND/BACKEND, RAW_INFERENCE_PROXY_FRONTEND/BACKEND, ...), each with a fixed socket pattern and a defined bind/connect side."
    }

    points: [
      "Event bus: XPUB/XSUB, proxied inside SystemController — every service PUBs to the frontend, SUBs from the backend.",
      "Dataset requests: DEALER/ROUTER proxy — workers' fallback path to ask dataset_manager for a conversation on demand.",
      "Raw inference results: PUSH/PULL proxy — workers push results fire-and-forget toward the record pipeline.",
      "Credit dispatch (ROUTER/DEALER) and credit return (dedicated PUSH/PULL) are NOT proxied — bound directly by timing_manager."
    ]

    caption: "The credit channels bypass the proxy layer entirely — bound straight into timing_manager."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s6-hdr",
        title = "FIVE PATTERNS, FIVE JOBS",
