  slide "AIPerf: stop conditions are ANDed" {
    eyebrow: "AIPerf architecture"
    title: "Five StopCondition classes; every applicable one must agree"
    lede: "StopConditionChecker builds only the subset of conditions whose should_use(config) is true for this phase, then combines them with AND — every active condition has to independently permit sending, every time, before the next request goes out."

    narration: "AIPerf defines five StopCondition subclasses: two lifecycle conditions that are always active, and three optional ones — request count, session count, and duration — that switch on only when their corresponding config field is set. StopConditionChecker evaluates should_use for each at phase start and keeps only the ones that apply, then can_send_any_turn is implemented as all(func() for func in self._can_send_any_turn_funcs) — a plain Python all(), meaning AND, not OR. There's no scenario where one permissive condition overrides a stricter one; every active condition has to agree before a request can go out. Request-count itself opts out entirely when overshoot-poll mode is configured, handing the stop decision to a different mechanism instead."

    term: {
      word: "StopConditionChecker"
      meaning: "AIPerf's aggregator over every StopCondition whose should_use(config) is true for the current phase. Combines them with a plain Python all() — AND logic — so every applicable condition must independently permit continuing before the phase sends another request."
    }

    points: [
      "Always active: LifecycleStopCondition (cancellation/sending-complete), DagLifecycleStopCondition (DAG-child cancellation gate).",
      "Conditionally active: RequestCountStopCondition, SessionCountStopCondition, DurationStopCondition — only when their config field is set.",
      "can_send_any_turn() = all(f() for f in active_funcs) — every applicable condition must agree, no OR anywhere in the checker.",
      "RequestCountStopCondition.should_use returns False when overshoot_poll_interval_sec is set — it hands off entirely."
    ]

    caption: "Every applicable condition votes; any one no-vote stops the phase."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s8-hdr",
        title = "ALL() — NOT ANY()",
        caption = "Every applicable condition votes; any one no-vote stops the phase.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.secondary),
        inkRole = theme(ink.secondary)
